    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Design and operations must converge on one canonical location per concern.",
      "excerpt_char_count": 74,
      "heading": "1) Single Source of Truth",
      "line_number": 13,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_13a21608c9dd19e832e4",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "- Do not duplicate state across parallel stores when one canonical store is sufficient. - Do not create shadow memory systems, side ledgers, or mirrored docs that can drift. - Prefer native project files and unified data stores over external synchronization layers. - If redundancy is unavoidable for reliability, define one canonical writer and deterministic reconciliation rules.",
      "excerpt_char_count": 381,
      "heading": "1) Single Source of Truth",
      "line_number": 15,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_594156e427005c7644b8",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "2) Minimalist Infrastructure (Code Over Bloat)",
      "excerpt_char_count": 46,
      "heading": "2) Minimalist Infrastructure (Code Over Bloat)",
      "line_number": 20,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_3aa6357c0c13e52af95d",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "Prefer simple, inspectable code paths over heavyweight orchestration frameworks.",
      "excerpt_char_count": 80,
      "heading": "2) Minimalist Infrastructure (Code Over Bloat)",
      "line_number": 22,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_3e4db8f6c9dc9ec40291",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "- Start with standard functions, small queues, native schedulers, and direct scripts. - Avoid adding visual orchestration stacks or complex abstraction layers unless strictly necessary. - Optimize for low operational overhead and fast incident diagnosis. - Every new moving part must have a clear failure model and maintenance owner.",
      "excerpt_char_count": 333,
      "heading": "2) Minimalist Infrastructure (Code Over Bloat)",
      "line_number": 24,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_a25c1b62fae70f40e8ef",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "3) Audit Before Adding",
      "excerpt_char_count": 22,
      "heading": "3) Audit Before Adding",
      "line_number": 29,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_4b325d42f1459650399b",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "No new dependency or system layer is introduced without proving existing capabilities are insufficient.",
      "excerpt_char_count": 103,
      "heading": "3) Audit Before Adding",
      "line_number": 31,
      "markdown_evidence_item_id": "mdeitem_cf7b1c8db9f65b6aa456",
      "parsed_evidence_not_truth": 1,
      "source_path": "CORE_ARCHITECTURE_PRINCIPLES.md",
      "truth_claimed": 0
    },
    {
      "evidence_category": "doctrine_or_system_map",
      "evidence_label": "doctrine_excerpt",
      "excerpt": "- First audit what the current stack can already do. - Use existing native features when they satisfy the requirement. - Add new tools only when there is a verified capability gap. - Record the gap, alternatives considered, and decision rationale in the relevant project log.",
      "excerpt_char_count": 275,
      "heading": "3) Audit Before Adding",
      "line_number": 33,
